WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.520
Weak encryption undermines the confidentiality customers expect from a SaaS provider.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.540
Teams should avoid outdated algorithms, custom cryptography, hard-coded secrets,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.440
poor randomness, and weak password hashing practices.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.780
Missing or misconfigured TLS can expose credentials, session tokens, API traffic,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.760
and customer data in transit.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.940
Secure certificate handling and modern transport settings must be consistent across web

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.160
apps, APIs, services, and integrations.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.980
Poor key management can defeat otherwise strong encryption.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.800
Keys need protected storage, limited access, rotation, lifecycle management,

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.180
and separation from the data they protect.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.600
Sensitive data exposure can also happen through logs, exports, backups, debug output,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.260
cached responses, and excessive API responses.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.320
Applications should minimize sensitive data and control where it appears.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.420
Use strong encryption standards and vetted libraries.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.920
Handle certificates and TLS configuration securely.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.740
Manage keys through protected, access-controlled processes.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.800
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC6.7 - Data protection;

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.460
CC6.8 - Transmission protection.
